{"id":5836,"date":"2020-10-13T13:43:54","date_gmt":"2020-10-13T13:43:54","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.jammindjs.net\/?p=5836"},"modified":"2020-10-13T13:43:54","modified_gmt":"2020-10-13T13:43:54","slug":"how-to-find-your-dj-wedding-edition","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.jammindjs.net\/blog\/how-to-find-your-dj-wedding-edition\/","title":{"rendered":"How to Find Your DJ: Wedding Edition"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In this blog, we talk a lot about what makes a great DJ. Over the next few weeks we\u2019ll be taking a look at how and where to FIND the perfect DJ for your event.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">When it comes to choosing a DJ for your wedding, there are some very specific qualities that you should consider. Your wedding day will likely be one of the most important and memorable days of your life, so why would you entrust an amateur with the entertainment? A great wedding DJ is experienced, professional, knowledgeable, and flexible, so it\u2019s important that you put ample thought into how you go about finding the right person.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As with any search, the internet is a great place to start. There are entire websites devoted to helping engaged couples find every vendor necessary to make your wedding and reception as beautiful and memorable as possible. Websites like Wedding Wire and The Knot are an amazing place to START. They have an amazing list of talented hosts and DJ\u2019s and even allow for users to rate each vendor after each event. Both sites also give out awards to vendors so that users have an idea of which companies to start with. Jammin\u2019 DJ\u2019s has won a plethora of awards for both and was recently named to The Knot\u2019s Hall of Fame!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Social Media is also an amazing place to look. Any entertainment company worth its salt is going to have a strong social media presence on Facebook and Instagram. Additionally, ask around. If you can remember a wedding at which you thoroughly enjoyed the music and vibe, ask the bride or groom who they hired and where they found them.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Lastly, and most importantly, DO YOUR RESEARCH. How many DJ\u2019s does the company have? Which of their DJ\u2019s has performed at the most weddings? Is their equipment state-of-the art? These are all important questions that you should know the answers to BEFORE you hire anyone. Truthfully, the best advice I can give you is to actually SPEAK with your prospective entertainer and GO TO A PERFORMANCE at another event. Interviewing your candidate is an essential step in any hiring process because it works. Hiring blind is never a good idea, and I promise that you\u2019ll feel much more comfortable with your choice after you get to have a conversation about your wants and needs. The right DJ wants for your wedding and reception to succeed, so if there\u2019s anything that they\u2019re uncomfortable with or incapable of, they\u2019ll let you know, and might be able to recommend the DJ that\u2019s right for you.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Following all of these steps is the most tried and true way of finding the DJ that\u2019s right for you. We\u2019re all rooting for you, so go out there and do it!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.theknot.com\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">www.theknot.com<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> | <\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.weddingwire.com\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">www.weddingwire.com<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>In this blog, we talk a lot about what makes a great DJ. Over the next few weeks we\u2019ll be taking a look at how and where to FIND the perfect DJ for your event.\u00a0 When it comes to choosing a DJ for your wedding, there are some very specific qualities